gates and these
passages!␀Well.␀The gates
of Jhelom.␀These passages
are restricted.␀A␀A␀A␀GATE␀PASS␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Aesop␀He␀A small man.␀I search
for valor!␀Well enough.␀I find that 'tis
easy to be brave
from a safe
distance!␀The mantra of
valor is 'RA'
use it in the
shrine on the
next isle!␀Know what
I mean?␀Thats my
problem.␀Thou art brave!␀VALO␀MANT␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Gravnor␀He␀A grave fighter.␀I search the
dungeons.␀So so.␀I seek the
red stone.␀It is found on
an altar!␀Dost thou
have it?␀No wonder I
can't find it!␀It lies in the
dungeon Destard!␀DUNG␀STON␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Senora␀She␀A beautiful mage␀I am locked up
in this tower.␀Well enough.␀I am being
punished for my
crimes.␀Does not matter,
I can help thee!␀Dost thou have
a ship?␀Then thou dost
need a sextant
ask the barkeep
for he knows
more!␀Too bad.␀TOWE␀CRIM␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Nostro␀He␀A withering soul␀I built these
passages and
they walled
me in!␀Very near death!␀This passage
runs around the
city!␀The rune is
buried in a
tower!␀Wilt thou lead
me out?␀I am saved!␀Thou art a cad!
and I will still
follow!␀PASS␀RUNE␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Luke␀He␀A ranger with a
far away look.␀I seek the
inner light!␀Quite well.␀I come from
Skara Brae and
am on my way to
Yew.␀'tis a city
based in the
virtue of
justice!␀Hast thou been
to Skara Brae?␀A fine city!␀'tis a spiritual
city!␀LIGH␀YEW ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Max␀He␀The housekeeper.␀I am the
housekeeper.␀Good!␀I clean
the rooms.␀That's a strange
one at the
end. People
often disappear.␀Is there some
problem with thy
room?␀I am very sorry
I will correct
it right away!␀Oh, thou had
me worried!␀HOUS␀ROOM␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀X␀He␀A strange person␀I seek the stone␀O.K.␀The red stone.␀Red is for valor
a virtue of the
